// Negative (review regression, issue #285): the fuel/WCET cost model must
// charge a runtime-address physical write like the volatile store it compiles
// to: address expression (1 for a literal) + value expression (1) + the store
// instruction (1) = 3, plus the `return` (1). A `[ fuel 1; ]` bound must
// therefore FAIL. Before the fix, RuntimePhysWriteExpr fell through to the
// leaf default priced at 0 instructions, so this function verified at 1 —
// unsound for the M3 fuel/WCET guarantee (issue #262) on exactly the fb.c
// pixel-write code this builtin unblocks.
fn poke(pm: cap phys.mem) -> Unit
  [ fuel 1; ]
{
  unsafe {
    phys_write_u32(1048576, 0xFF8800);
  }
  return;
}
